From: koalabuttz <27229333+koalabuttz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 06:12:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: stop an OpenAL source before taking its buffer away

SND_ReleaseChannelBuffer set AL_BUFFER to 0 on a source that could
still be playing, then deleted the buffer. OpenAL refuses both on a
playing or paused source (AL_INVALID_OPERATION), so a sound that was
cut short or had its channel stolen kept playing, its buffer leaked,
and the next sound on that channel never attached: alSourcePlay
replayed the old one. In play this is heard as sounds that drop out or
repeat.

Rewind the source first, as AIL_end_sample does in the Miles driver.
Rewind leaves it AL_INITIAL, so a start that is delayed or paused is
not taken for a finished sound. Run against OpenAL Soft's loopback
device, the old code keeps the old tone and the new code plays the next
one. Part of upstream issue 76.
---
 src/sound/snd_driver_openal.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/sound/snd_driver_openal.cpp b/src/sound/snd_driver_openal.cpp
index 7771d989..83c3e528 100644
--- a/src/sound/snd_driver_openal.cpp
+++ b/src/sound/snd_driver_openal.cpp
@@ -97,6 +97,8 @@ void SND_ReleaseChannelBuffer(int index)
 {
     if (alGlob.channelBuffer[index])
     {
+        // A playing or paused source keeps its buffer; stop it first.
+        alSourceRewind(alGlob.source[index]);
         alSourcei(alGlob.source[index], AL_BUFFER, 0);
         alDeleteBuffers(1, &alGlob.channelBuffer[index]);
         alGlob.channelBuffer[index] = 0;
